alternatives: A continuous fill beneath the ceiling would obstruct upward finger entry. Sloping the working ceiling would replace the flat lifting bearing with a ramp. Extra roof thickness extending downward would reduce the defined hand space; the retained 12 mm roof and its complete supporting posts already occupy their intended load path.
