[sliver] The two rounded handhold-rim picks belong to degenerate STL facets with zero normals and undefined strip dimensions. They do not identify a finite thin wall or a material ledge. The post-publication bounded face-class receipt in y-seam-plain-review.json records these exact picks on the uncovered back-bottom mesh.
alternatives: A different tessellation can omit degenerate facets without changing the material boundary. Thickening or squaring the native rounded rim would change the gripping surface without addressing a finite thin section at these picks.
