[ceiling] These are the two lower faces of back-bottom's second Y-seam screw-bearing blocks, at Z102.15. Each block retains its complete 35.95 mm height and roots into the rear flank beyond the interleaving fingers. The 0.5 mm gaps beside the mating front blocks stay open after seating; this face is not a compression spacer. Tree(auto)/Default is the starting support treatment. With the part separate, the seam and interior expose the support beneath the block; cleanup effort remains unqualified.
alternatives: A corbel below the face would occupy the mating front block's insertion space. A sloped block end would reduce the printed screw-bearing length. Joining the blocks with a continuous post would prevent the two halves from interleaving.
