[ceiling] These Z37.25 faces are the lower screws' flat washer-bearing floors. Each 8 mm head pocket opens toward the interior, with a printed 5.6 mm screw passage and a complete bearing annulus for the 10 mm washer. The native head-seat witness retains 3 mm of stock behind that annulus; the cover-removal relation preserves it. Tree(auto)/Default is the starting support treatment. Support leaves through the open pocket and handhold before the loose washer and screw are installed; cleanup and washer-handling ease remain unqualified.
alternatives: Sloping the floor would tilt the flat washer and screw head. A shallower pocket would reduce the specified head recess or change the screw's seating plane and reach. Closing the inward opening would retain the unnecessary thin inboard cup wall.
